A||N||13||DaRkLoRD||Hot air into the engine?||||5||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||02-15-2001||01:58 AM||||I know the Fiero uses cold air intakes, and sucking in warm air won't give the best performance... I know a few people who have a K&N filter bolted right to the 2.8 TB, and a couple of people with flat air cleaners on top of the duke.. is this just inefficient, or could it hurt the engine?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||02-15-2001||02:41 AM||||Just inefficient.  Especially in the Fiero's engine compartment.  Not much air movement and too much heat.  Won't hurt the engine, but you'll lose a bit of performance.  The duke does look a helluva lot better with a flat air cleaner, imho.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||02-15-2001||10:26 AM||||Can't remember who's car it was, but someone had the K&N down in the fender well with side scoops. (Must be an all day job to take it out for cleaning)??? but there must be some improvememt with this type set up??<BR>That's what I'm thinking about doing.<P>What about the "Cold Air Intake" that Fiero Store sells??? Anyone have it?<P><BR>Steve, you should be getting a package in the mail soon  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||02-15-2001||12:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>The duke does look a helluva lot better with a flat air cleaner, imho.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's why I asked.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||02-15-2001||01:04 PM||||It was Shaun Hammit who had that custom Cold Air Intake.  I think he said he gained some Hp but lost some torque.  Pretty innovative if you ask me.<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/fierogtnos/intake.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||02-15-2001||01:45 PM||||Yep! That's the one. Black88 you got a link to his site???<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000006||Black88GT||02-15-2001||02:17 PM||||Sure do...<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/fierogtnos" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/fierogtnos</A> <P><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000007||286SE'S||02-15-2001||03:23 PM||||Yes, I want that! That piece of string holding it up looks great.<BR>I had read that heated air gives better burn characteristics to the gas and fuel economy is much better. That is the theory behind those 100mpg carbs that were around in the late 70's. A guy at work was getting over 50 mpg with his Ford Pinto with some simple heating mods. Wasn't there just a thread on gas mileage that everyone agreed that summer is better for MPG?||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||02-15-2001||03:45 PM||||286SE'S, I have a scanned magazine article somewhere about a high mileage Fiero that uses heated air.. the guy's name was Smokey something.. last name started with a Y..<P>the other trick to high mileage is completely vaporizing the gasoline, and mixing it fully with the incoming air. Only gasoline vapors will burn completely, not droplets.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000009||Alex4mula||02-15-2001||03:55 PM||||Cold air = more dense = more O2. I like that setup but what I won't like is taking it out for cleaning. Someone should sell a kit for that.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||02-16-2001||12:26 AM||||The guy doing the experiments was Smokey Yunick. I remember reading about some of his experiments. Don't specifically remember the Fiero, though.<BR>I wonder what happened to the project. Maybe the oil companies paid him off to shut up. <BR>(I'm <I>not</I> cynical. Really, I'm not.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||02-16-2001||01:04 AM||||Okay, Check this link... <A HREF="http://www.himacresearch.com/letters/feedback.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.himacresearch.com/letters/feedback.htm</A> <BR>It's a series of e-mails regarding "heated fuel" experiments.<BR>There are also several other sites.<BR>Do a net search using "yunick hot vapor", and see what you come up with.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||02-16-2001||01:21 AM||||Bruce McBurney has some awesome stuff on his website, as does George Wiseman at <A HREF="http://www.eagle-research.com" TARGET=_blank>www.eagle-research.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
